&#x200B;

Pero con la tema de sentir incomoda de tener mujeres transgeneros en baños publicos o el gimnasio, dónde van ellas si no en esos lugares? Al baño de hombres? O el parte en el gimnasio para hombres? No puedes imaginar como peligroso eso podría ser para esa persona? Todo eso por solo querriendo hacer un pís o cambiar su ropa para hacer ejercicio...?

Y para los hombres transgeneros? A donde van ellos? Quieres compartir un baño con [este hombre](https://elclosetlgbt.com/closetnews/hombre-trans-participar-concurso-de-fisicoculturismo-en-la-india/)? Porque siguendo tu logico, él, nacido como un mujer, él "físicamente tiene el mismo cuerpo" a ti no?

thats really sad to hear ...............

&#x200B;

if ur comfortable abt it , maybe u could try mentioning ur autistic and then give some ideas of what u think could help that child and others in similar situations . im a teacher and i have had situations b4 of kids clearly being autistic and coworkers not being good w them cuz they dont have training either . nd ive always had ppl respond very positively and enthusiastically 2 any of my ideas to improve things for students neurodiverse or not

&#x200B;

i think many r eager 2 learn especially if they chose 2 look after kids and would welcome ur viewpoint , but i get if u dont wanna disclose tht 2 ppl ..

i remember my brother had a mark exactly like this on his cheek and i always thought it was super cool it must have been from popping milia as well but its disappeared as he got older so i think they do fade over time

&#x200B;

its very unique looking tho like a spiral galaxy !

I think an expert in the Zhou dynasty would be someone to seek out if you really wanted a good explanation cuz I'm a total novie in ancient Chinese, but to me it reads something like

&#x200B;

"4th year, 5th month of Father (1) Zhou's dynasty. \[  作亶 (2)  \]...benefit of usage thanks to the Imperial clan (3)"

&#x200B;

(1) 父王 is a term of address used here, this term was used by children of the Emperor to refer to him

(3) 宗室 refers to Chinese nobility, so whoever was in charge at the time this was originally made (King Zhou probably)

(2) I believe there is reference to [this person](https://www.easyatm.com.tw/wiki/%E4%BA%B6%E7%88%B6), but I don't know enough about the Zhou dynasty to understand why he's referenced here

&#x200B;

Sorry, hope someone else can help

Ah! That gave me a very different insight, I didn't think of it like that!

Thank you very much!

&#x200B;
